8828 | Page 350 | {} | Recd 740 PM  Lynchburg Va Sept 30. 1865  / 730 pm Hon T. T. Eckert  In the absence of Genl / Curtis I have notified Capt. Alberger & others / ---- they left on the train this P / M & will be in Washn tomorrow morning / A. S. S. Foote Capt. AAG . /  /  / Recd 12 M Oct 1.  Hilton Head / Maj Eckert  / Just returned from interior of State ---- will send / report of supplies recd from Am. Tel. Co. by mail ---- / I have between 8 & 10 thousand dolls rects / belonging to Am Tel. Co to whom shall I send it ? / J. R. Gilmore Capt &c /  /  / 3 pm  New Orleans Oct 18 65  / Hd Qrs Mily Div of the Gulf N Orleans Oct 18 10 am / EM Stanton Secy War . Gen Steele communicates the following  / intelligence . Isaac Surratt , an other son of  / Mrs Surratt left Montery Mexico some three / or four weeks ago to assassinate the President / . this resolution was taken after he heard of the  / execution of his mother , and the rebels of that / place made up a purse for him the / young man was very frantic when he left Monterey / some four weeks ago travelling toward the Rio Grande on / horse back . Isaac Surratt , is about 30 / two years of age , olive complexion , five / feet nine or ten inches in height full  / beard dark eyes . black curly hair and good / looking . was a member of Duffs Regt of / Cavalry . / PH Sheridan / 
8830 | Page 352 | {} | 730 pm 26  New Orleans 11 AM Oct 26. 1865 / New Orleans Oct 26th 11 AM Secy of War / Gen Foster has made a personal inspection of / Tortuga in compliance with my directions to ascertain / the facts of the attempted escape of Dr Mudd / . He puts the blame on the men of the / one hundred & sixty first NY Vols now mustered  / out & exhonorates the Comdg officer of the Fort . / the garrison at the fort has been changed . I forward / Foster report by mail  PH Sheridan / M Gen /  /  / 1 pm 29th  New Orleans Oct 28 1865 / Hd Qrs Octo 28th 930 am for Secy of War . Mr / John K Spires the man from whom the information / was obtained of the intention of Isaac Surrat / ---- stepped off from me on the US steam ship  / Mariposa which sailed for N York on the evening of the 26th / from this place . He is unconscious of the Govt  / being in possession of the information that was obtained from / him through Mr Attril . I hesitated to arrest  / him here fearing it might interfere with the arrest / of Surrat but he has registered his name  / on the ships Register and can be apprehended at N York on the / arrival of the boat . I think he is on his / way to Canada ( message of 27 10 am just rec'd ) / P. H. Sheridan / M Gen / 
8693 | Page 215 | {} | 11 am  Fort Monroe Apl 17 1865 / Hd Qrs C A Apl 14th to Gen Sherman Genl . The  / results of the recent Campaign in Va have so changed / the relative military conditions of the belligerants I am therefore / induced to address you in this form the inquiry whether / in order to stop further effusion of blood & destruction / of property you are willing to make a temporary suspension / of active operations & to communicate to Gen Grant / comdg the armies of the you S the request that he / will take like action in regard to otherse the object / being to permit the civil authorities to enter / into the need - full arrangements to terminate  / the existing war . I have the honor to be very  / Respyfy Your Obt Svt  J E Johnston Genl /  /  / GJ Lawrence Balto  Fort Monroe Apl 17 / Ft Monroe 17th JL McPhail Pro Mar Genl  / &c Balto I have arrested Saml Arnold you will arrest  / J W Booth and Michael Laughlin of / Balto G W Aszrodt alias Port Tobacco of / Charles County & John Surrett residence not known as all / are implicated V Randall / 
